  "failures": [],
  "frame": "1 Blender unit = 1 stud. The tip is at the origin and the cue runs along Blender -Y (tip to butt); the glTF exporter (+Y up) maps Blender (x, y, z) to glTF (x, z, -y), so the cue runs along glTF/Roblox local +Z with the tip at z = 0. The UV seam is at theta = 0, Blender -Z = Roblox local -Y (down in the hand). theta runs seam -> +X -> +Z (top) -> -X. Studio (checked 2026-09-29): Roblox's glTF importer turns the model 180 degrees about Y and centres the MeshPart on its bounds, so in the MeshPart the tip is at local +Z = length / 2 and the seam still at -Y; PivotOffset = CFrame.new(0, 0, length / 2) * CFrame.Angles(0, pi, 0) puts the pivot on the tip with +Z toward the butt.",
